title Cassette bound (studio input): 44.1 kHz chosen, then the Opus codec: the rate moves to 48 kHz and a line names it; the Bit rate picker; Opus dims 44.1 and 96 kHz in the Sample rate picker
sizes 480x320 320x480 640x480
ppmm 608
env CASSETTE_DEMO 1
env CASSETTE_DEMO_HOME demo-home
env CASSETTE_DEMO_CARD rich
env CASSETTE_DEMO_CODECS both
env CASSETTE_LAYOUT_CHECK 1

wait 1500
key s
wait 500
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key enter
wait 500
key up
key enter
wait 800
expect text "44.1 kHz"
shot settings-44k
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key down
key down
key down
key down
key enter
wait 500
key down
key down
key enter
wait 800
expect text "Sample rate set to 48 kHz: Opus cannot record at 44.1 kHz"
shot settings-opus-toast
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
say the line stays a few seconds; the footer of the next page shows when it has gone
wait 4500
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
wait 300
expect text "Bit rate"
shot settings-opus-rows
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key up
key enter
wait 500
expect text "Opus needs 8, 12, 16, 24 or 48 kHz"
expect text "Sizes for Opus, 32 kbps, this card"
shot rate-opus
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key down
key enter
wait 300
expect text "Not available: Opus needs 8, 12, 16, 24 or 48 kHz"
shot rate-opus-notice
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key esc
wait 300
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key down
key enter
wait 500
shot bitrate-picker
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key down
key down
key enter
wait 800
expect text "64 kbps"
shot settings-64
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
expect noquit
